## 3. SDLC Process (Adopted Going Forward)

Given the current solo/AI-assisted development model, a **lightweight Agile/Kanban hybrid** is recommended — full Scrum ceremonies would be overhead for the current team size, but the *artifacts and gates* of a formal SDLC are still required because this is a financial/automotive marketplace handling PII, payments-adjacent data, and dealer business documents.

### 3.1 Phases

| Phase | Activities | Gate to next phase |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Requirements & Planning** | Investor/PM define feature scope in this file under §5 (Backlog). Each item gets an owner, acceptance criteria. | PM sign-off on scope |
| **2. Design** | Schema changes drafted as a numbered migration in `supabase/migrations/`. UI changes follow design system in README. | PM + Tech Lead review |
| **3. Implementation** | Feature branch per task (`feature/<area>-<short-desc>`). | Self-review + lint pass |
| **4. QA / Verification** | Manual test against acceptance criteria + relevant automated tests (once test suite exists). Update `QA_REPORT.md`. | QA sign-off, no new HIGH/CRITICAL |
| **5. Release** | Merge to `main`, apply any pending migrations via Supabase SQL Editor or CLI, deploy via Vercel. | PM approval **required** before any `git push` to `main`, Supabase migration, or production deploy (per existing investor preference) |
| **6. Monitor & Retro** | Check `/api/health`, error logs (once Sentry added), update this file's §7 conversation log with outcomes. | — |

### 3.2 Branching & Release Policy
- `main` = production-tracking branch. **No direct commits.**
- All work happens on `feature/*` or `fix/*` branches.
- PM (Claude) drafts PRs; Investor or designated reviewer approves merges to `main`.
- Migrations are versioned, sequential, and **never edited after being applied** — only new migrations may alter existing tables.

### 3.3 Definition of Done (DoD)
A task is "Done" only when:
- [ ] Code implemented and matches acceptance criteria
- [ ] No new lint errors (`npm run lint`)
- [ ] Manually verified against the running app (per `verify` skill standards — real browser/API call, not just code read)
- [ ] README and/or this file updated to reflect the change
- [ ] No secrets committed
- [ ] PM has logged the change in §7 of this file

