## 6. Governance, Policy & Licensing

### 6.1 Confidentiality
- This file (`memory.me`) and `CHATGPT_SCHEMA_PROMPT.md` contain architectural details that should be treated as **confidential business information**. Do not paste into public ChatGPT sessions without first stripping real project identifiers (project ref IDs, real emails, etc.) — the schema prompt as written is safe (no secrets), but always review before pasting externally.
- Service role keys, API keys, and access tokens must **never** appear in this file, in commits, or in chat transcripts that leave this environment. If a key is ever pasted into a session accidentally, it must be **rotated immediately** in the Supabase dashboard.

### 6.2 Intellectual Property
- All code, designs, schema, and documentation produced under this engagement are **work product owned by the Investor** unless otherwise agreed in writing.
- Third-party dependencies (Next.js, Supabase, Anthropic SDK, OpenAI SDK, etc.) remain under their respective open-source/commercial licenses — see `package.json` for the full dependency list. No copyleft (GPL) dependencies currently identified; verify during S1-4 audit.
- The "This is NOT the Next.js you know" note in `AGENTS.md` is a project-specific instruction to consult `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for this Next.js version's actual API — **not** a license or legal notice. No action needed from a governance perspective, but engineers must follow it to avoid building against incorrect/training-data APIs.

### 6.3 Data Protection & Compliance
- GDPR consent tracking exists (`consent_records`, `lib/privacy/`) — good foundation.
- **Policy:** No real customer PII should be used in development/testing environments. Use synthetic data only (the `data/` seed files and `QA_REPORT.md` dummy listings are appropriate).
- **Policy:** Any dealer verification documents (`dealer_documents`, once migrated) contain sensitive business documents (FCA authorisation, VAT certs) — storage bucket access must remain service-role-only, never public.

### 6.4 Release & Change Control (reaffirms existing memory)
- **PM must obtain explicit Investor approval before:** `git push` to any shared branch, applying database migrations to the live Supabase project, merging PRs to `main`, or any production deployment. *(This restates the existing "Deploy Confirmation" policy already in memory — it is now formalized here as governance, not just a preference.)*
- **No destructive database operations** (`DROP TABLE`, `TRUNCATE`, force migrations) without a verified backup and explicit Investor sign-off.

### 6.5 Documentation Policy (reaffirms existing memory)
- Every functional change to the platform must be reflected in `README.md` (developer-facing) **and** this `memory.me` file (investor/governance-facing) in the same working session it is made. *(Restates existing "README Docs Rule" memory, extended to cover this file.)*

